{
 "about": "The learning path's units: our own grouping of the games' words into scenes from a child's day, the idea (and these Yorùbá titles) borrowed from the curriculum draft, which is a draft for one teacher-led course and not a template for the games. Each scene lists its words by id, in teaching order (verbs early where the scene allows; every compound after its parts, which the builder enforces anyway). suggestedBy names the curriculum units whose items mark a word as the curriculum's (● on the path page); the builder reports curriculum words that are in no scene. A second visit (secondOf) is planned, not a leftover: it comes back to its scene later in the path with that scene's later words. A scene with hold waits (its words are tracked, no stones). held: words kept off the path on purpose, with the reason. Words no game can show yet are listed too, so they are tracked as waiting. apart: never two of a pair in one sitting's new words or in one stone (look-alike pictures, or one meaning). Revised 2026-11-20 after the pre-deploy audit: ten units (Day, Body, Animals early, Meal, Feelings, Washing, Family, Home with the fire words before ìdáná, Play and outdoors, Dressed held until wọ̀ has a picture) and four planned second visits.",
